[GPU fmod C2C read/write validation]


Since our run uses the simfront backend (BackdoorMemSimFront), so GPU‑HBM writes go through a direct mmap pointer and never call BackdoorMemWrite. The flag check is never reached → no logs, by design of that config.
So even we use GDB to change the debug variables mem_debug_reads/write, we still cannot expect to see backdoor memory read/write logs.




[Backdoor C2C] (Disable GPU ATS and IOMMU)

#1. Remove the stale RM
rmmod nvidia_drm; rmmod nvidia_modeset; rmmod nvidia; rmmod nvidia_vgpu_vfio


#2. Load the RM with below regkeys
sudo bash nvload_rm.sh -v -d -b gr102_sim_hbm3.rom -r 'RMDisableAcr=0x1;RmPowerFeature=0x55555555;RMPowerFeature2=0x55555555;RMNvLinkControl=0x1;EnableMSI=0;RmDevinitDmaUseSPA=0x1;RmDefaultTimeout=0x10000;RmPmuBootstrapMode=0x1;RmDisableCtxswUcodeFromChiplib=1;RMForceNetlistNumber=2;RmOverrideSelfHostedMode=0x1;RmOverrideC2CLinks=0x1;RmOverrideCoherentCpuFbBase=0x2000;RmOverrideNonPasidAtsSupport=0x0;EnableUserNUMAManagement=0;CoherentGPUMemoryMode=driver'

#3. Disable the WDT
sudo sysctl -w kernel.watchdog_thresh=0

